<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Exp Med</journal-id><journal-title>The Journal of Experimental Medicine</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0022-1007</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1540-9538</issn><publisher><publisher-name>The Rockefeller University Press</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">19867469</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2124772</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Article</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>THE EFFECT OF SALVARSAN UPON THE HEART IN DOGS</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Auer</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name></contrib></contrib-group><aff id="N0x1ce4210N0x1d8f2f0">From the Department of Physiology and Pharmacology of the Rockefeller Institute for Medical Research, New York.</aff><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><day>1</day><month>9</month><year>1911</year></pub-date><volume>14</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>248</fpage><lpage>255</lpage><history><date date-type="received"><day>20</day><month>6</month><year>1911</year></date></history><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; Copyright, 1911, by The Rockefeller Institute for Medical Research New York</copyright-statement></permissions><abstract><p> The intravenous infusion of 0.5 per cent. <italic>acid</italic> "606" causes a weakening of the heart which is usually fatal. The intravenous infusion of 0.5 per cent. <italic>alkaline</italic> "606" causes no marked apparent effect upon the heart, but its factors of safety may be so reduced in some instances that a slight extra strain produces fibrillation and death. </p></abstract></article-meta></front></article>